WEBVTT

NOTE creating-profiles: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.984
Capture the station
targets you have tuned,

V0-2
00:00:05.084 --> 00:00:07.370
under a name you will
recognise next season.

V1a-1
00:00:13.303 --> 00:00:16.790
A profile is a snapshot, so the
work happens in the table before

V1a-2
00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.268
you save anything. Get the course
reading the way you want it,

V1a-3
00:00:20.368 --> 00:00:22.493
hole by hole, and only then capture it.

V1b-1
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:29.082
The Target VWC column is what a profile
would capture. A profile stores one Target

V1b-2
00:00:29.182 --> 00:00:34.590
VWC per station and nothing else,
no percent adjustments, no enable states.

V2a-1
00:00:41.323 --> 00:00:43.643
Open the Target Profiles tab in Settings.

V2b-1
00:00:44.606 --> 00:00:48.734
Profiles sit with the calculation
settings rather than in the table,

V2b-2
00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:53.146
because a target set is a calculation
input rather than a station edit.

V3a-1
00:00:59.816 --> 00:01:03.121
Name a profile for the reason
the targets are what they are:

V3a-2
00:01:03.221 --> 00:01:06.086
Summer Baseline, Tournament
Week, Overseed Recovery.

V3b-1
00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.973
A date tells you when;
a condition tells you why,

V3b-2
00:01:10.073 --> 00:01:12.460
which is what you will be searching for.

V4a-1
00:01:18.806 --> 00:01:22.677
The count beside each profile
says how many stations it covers.

V4a-2
00:01:22.777 --> 00:01:27.816
A profile holds every station the course
had when it was captured, enabled or not.

V4b-1
00:01:28.773 --> 00:01:32.537
Stations added to the course later
are not in it, and applying the

V4b-2
00:01:32.637 --> 00:01:36.573
profile leaves them untouched.
Coverage is part of what a profile is.
